# Agentic Adversary Readiness: APM (controls BIP-APM-01..05)
# Reference template. Validate in a lab.

# BIP-APM-02..04: session binding, lifetime and logon throttling on the access profile
modify apm profile access ap_vpn {
    restrict-to-single-client-ip true
    secure-cookie true
    httponly-cookie true
    inactivity-timeout 900
    max-session-timeout 43200
    max-in-progress-sessions 32
    max-concurrent-sessions 2
    min-failure-delay 2
    max-failure-delay 5
}

# BIP-APM-01: the second factor lives in the per-session policy (Visual Policy Editor), not in tmsh one-liners.
# Minimum acceptable order of preference:
#   1. On-Demand / machine certificate check, or SAML/OIDC to an IdP enforcing FIDO2
#   2. RADIUS / OTP push after the AD or LDAP password check
# Also: add a "Client OS / posture" branch, and deny on fallback. Name policy items descriptively
# (for example act_radius_mfa) so that the validator's name-based heuristic can find them.

# BIP-APM-05: per-request policy for continuous authorization, attached to the access virtual server
modify ltm virtual vs_vpn per-flow-request-access-policy prp_continuous_authz

# After any access policy change:
modify apm profile access ap_vpn generation-action increment
